The FESEM images show the microstructure of laccase-decorated lumen surface for biocatalytic NF membranes (Fig. 3

                        ). The LBL membrane presents a rough and compact lumen surface with irregular topography (Fig. 3A), which is in agreement with previously reported results [18]. After laccase immobilization, more protuberances on the surface can be identified. Furthermore, insignificant change to the lumen surface (Fig. 3B–D) and cross-section structures (Fig. A2) are observed, regardless of the laccase immobilization strategies. AFM images corroborate these results by showing increased roughness (R

                           a
                        ) from 10.79 ± 1.35 nm for LBL membrane to around 17.50 nm for biocatalytic NF membranes (Fig. A3). Together, these characterizations indicate a full coverage of laccase by polyelectrolyte deposition on the lumen surface.
